From 6a143f77629f9376c137dd1c894a97b7a8de15ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 01:39:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The Barrows chest pays into a window, and the last door asks
 a question

The last two of Corey's seven.

THE REWARD WINDOW. The chest used to pay into the chatbox and the inventory, which loses the point
of a run: you could not see what you got, and a full inventory quietly sent things to the bank. The
roll now drops into barrows_reward_store - scope=perm, eight slots - and the window IS that store,
an inv component, so the client draws the icons, the stack counts and the hover names for nothing
and its options come back as [inv_button1..3] with last_slot already filled in.

Eight slots is the ceiling on one chest: seven rolls at six brothers killed plus the teleport tabs.
tools/genbarrowschest.py reads that number out of the inv config rather than repeating it, so the
grid cannot end up smaller than the thing it draws. scope=perm because the alternative is losing
loot: a disconnect between the roll and the last click would drop a set piece out of a run that is
already over.

Take, Take-all and Bank per slot, a Take everything button, and CLOSING THE WINDOW BANKS WHATEVER
IS LEFT - the only ending that cannot cost a player a set piece. The store is flushed to the bank
BEFORE a new chest rolls, so the window only ever shows one chest's loot and there is always room
for it. The subtitle says how many rolls were made and at what reward potential, which is the one
thing about a Barrows reward a player cannot work out by looking.

Generated for the same reason the rift picker is - not the eight slots, but fifty-odd backing tiles
and border pieces plus interface.pack and interface.order having to agree on every component - and
the battery re-runs the generator and checks the .if AND BOTH PACKS come back byte-identical, which
is group 35's lesson.

THE PUZZLE DOOR, and it is words rather than shapes for a reason that is not a choice: the puzzle's
art is not in the 377 cache - the whole interface vocabulary here is bank buttons, borders, stat
icons and arrows, with nothing shape-like to draw a pattern from - and it cannot be imported from
this environment either, because SPRITE PACKING IS THE ONE PART OF THE BUILD THAT CANNOT RUN HERE
(the media and title archives are skipped, jimp being stubbed), so new interface art could be added
but never rendered or verified. A drawn puzzle is a round of its own on a machine that can pack
sprites. So the gate asks in the chat box with the sequence written out: the same puzzle, and the
same consequence for getting it wrong.

Eight of them, in %barrows_puzzle - the cache's own three bits, which nothing was using - rolled
with the maze and re-rolled every time the tunnels shift, so a wrong answer is not a free retry.
Each is a sequence with one symbol missing and four ways to finish it, and the right answer is in a
different position in each, because four puzzles whose answer is always the third option is one
puzzle. Written as eight switch cases rather than a table because a proc cannot return a string in
this codebase - battery check 24 enforces it - so the options cannot come out of an enum.

A wrong answer re-lays the maze, re-rolls the puzzle and locks the door again, and touches nothing
about the run itself: the brothers you killed stay killed and the reward potential stays earned.

AND WHICH GATES ASK IT IS MEASURED, NOT LISTED. The chest's own room is joined to the rest of the
tunnel by exactly four gates - e, i, j and l, the spokes of the cross - and barrowsmaze.py derives
that off maps/m55_151.jm2 so the battery checks the script's triggers against the map rather than
both reading a list somebody typed.

Verified: clean build, rs2check 1702 scripts / 491 configs with 0 ERROR and 0 CHECK, all eleven
batteries green, and barrows_battery.py's 852 checks against 198 mutations - each caught by its own
check. One fault worth keeping: a mutation to a GENERATOR can only ever be caught by byte-identity,
because the battery re-runs it before any other check reads its output - so a check about the
window's contents has to be mutation-tested from the script side instead.

